; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Rendered by Terraform (pgbouncer.tf) and mounted into the PgBouncer pod at
; /bitnami/pgbouncer/conf/userlist.txt, alongside pgbouncer.ini.tftpl.
;
; Plaintext-password entries ("user" "password") rather than pre-hashed
; SCRAM/MD5 secrets -- PgBouncer hashes them on the fly for both the
; client<->pgbouncer and pgbouncer<->postgres legs, and this is the ONLY
; format Terraform can populate without a second round-trip to read back
; each role's real rolpassword hash from a live Postgres after initdb runs.
; The plaintext value itself lives only in Terraform state (gitignored,
; same posture as every other generated password in this repo -- see
; postgres.tf's header) and in this rendered file inside a Kubernetes
; Secret, never in a tracked file.
;
; Every service's OWN role/password is listed here (needed so PgBouncer can
; open the real server-side connection to Postgres as that role) plus the
; Postgres superuser, which doubles as PgBouncer's admin_users entry for the
; `pgbouncer` pseudo-database admin console (SHOW POOLS etc., used by both
; the readiness probe and manual operator inspection).
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

"${admin_user}" "${admin_password}"
%{ for name, svc in services ~}
"${svc.user}" "${svc.password}"
%{ endfor ~}
